//? Title: Filter activations: full frozen VGG19 and every observed channel
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Learned convolutional filters and their responses to real images reveal different information. Inspect all 64 first-layer filters and all 2,944 channel maps from the complete frozen VGG19 network on the original Labrador and Kandinsky observations. Shared and local display scales make their different interpretations explicit.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/filter_activations.cpp`.

> The method

A learned convolution kernel is a fixed numerical operator. Its post-ReLU activation depends on the observed image and all preceding layers. Shared within-layer maximum scaling preserves relative amplitude across observations/channels; per-channel maximum scaling preserves only each map's visible pattern.

No model or image fitting occurs. All 32 official pretrained convolution arrays remain unchanged while all 16 original-width convolutions and max pools execute. The report retains raw values, independent numeric checks and every channel without selecting visually attractive examples.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/filter_activations_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/filter_activations_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/filter_activations_concept.tikz > build/filter_activations_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/filter_activations_concept.svg build/filter_activations_concept.dvi > build/filter_activations_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
