> Genuine original images and official frozen VGG19 weights

Use the original Yellow Labrador photograph by Wikimedia user Elf (CC BY-SA 3.0)
and Kandinsky's Composition VII (1913, public domain), the same source JPEGs as
the style-transfer reports. Source hashes, original URLs, attribution and the
pinned official Keras VGG19 no-top HDF5 hash remain in the preparation manifest.
Center-square crop with integer bounds, then tensor Float32 legacy bilinear interpolation to 64 px
and RGB/255. No synthetic substitute or learned input preprocessing is used.

All 16 original VGG19 convolutions execute with their original widths and max pools.
The 32 weight/bias arrays contain 20,024,384 official ImageNet learned values. There
is no classifier head, image optimization or fitting in this report; an optimizer
is therefore unnecessary. Unlike the style-transfer variant, the pooling path
is MAX rather than average. Raw activations are feature responses, not class
attributions or predictions about the two observations.

> Executed tensor architecture

Frozen VGG-19 uses zero constants only to probe the exact feature-extractor geometry here. Its constants are not learned leaves. The activation analyses below retain their actual pretrained weights.

This figure executes the inference configuration shown in the code, using a zero-valued
shape probe without fitting or loading a checkpoint. Named stage boundaries group
whole subgraphs where available; other nodes retain functional-layer detail. Exact
batch-inclusive shapes and reachable parameter totals come from the trace. Shared
linear scales map spatial dimensions and channel counts to blocks; the one-pixel
visibility floor is disclosed in the legend. Labels use compact monospace text,
rotate counterclockwise and sit beside their own glyphs. Arrows flow left to right;
wide diagrams scroll at native size on the website.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/filter_activations_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  m::TensorMap weights;
  int          input = 3;
  for (int b = 0; b < 5; ++b)
    for (int l = 0; l < m::FrozenVgg19::Depths[b]; ++l) {
      const auto name  = "block" + std::to_string(b + 1) + "_conv" + std::to_string(l + 1);
      const auto width = m::FrozenVgg19::Widths[b];
      weights.emplace(name + "_W", n::zeros({3, 3, input, width}));
      weights.emplace(name + "_b", n::zeros({width}));
      input = width;
    }
  const m::FrozenVgg19 vgg(weights);
  n::Module            architecture_model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& image) { return m::VggVisualFeatures(vgg, image).activation.back(); },
      "Filter activations: full frozen VGG19 and every observed channel");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.labels                = {.type = n::ModelPlotLabel::NameAndShape, .size = 12, .wrap = 24};
  options.spacing               = {.layer = 24, .lane = 12, .label = 8, .margin = 20};
  options.sizing.spatial_size   = 96;
  options.sizing.channel_size   = 42;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 1;
  options.opacity               = .8;
  const auto diagram            = architecture_model.plot(n::zeros({1, 64, 64, 3}), options);
  diagram.save_svg("build/filter_activations_architecture.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} displayed nodes; {} reachable learned values.\n",
      diagram.nodes().size(),
      diagram.parameter_count());
}
```
